(1118540, 134371, 28045, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all of your comments.  I actually dislike toy pictures myself but as I set this up in my head it kinda made me laugh thinking about it.  The entire shoot took about 2 hours because I continued shooting from various angles and with more and less toys in the picture.  I wanted to get a shot more from Ground level but when I would get the shot from that perspective it would make all the toys look like they were mixed together and the picture was very busy and it was a totally different effect that didnt show what I was trying to portray.  I couldnt get the lighting correct either because the there are alot of windows in the playroom and outside was cloudy and then sunny and it became frustrating trying to deal with so I just dialed in 1600 Iso and waited for a cloud to cover the sun. Over all I still am not crazy about the shot but it does make me LAUGH!</td>', 'Thanks for all of your comments.  I actually dislike toy pictures myself but as I set this up in my head it kinda made me laugh thinking about it.  The entire shoot took about 2 hours because I continued shooting from various angles and with more and less toys in the picture.  I wanted to get a shot more from Ground level but when I would get the shot from that perspective it would make all the toys look like they were mixed together and the picture was very busy and it was a totally different effect that didnt show what I was trying to portray.  I couldnt get the lighting correct either because the there are alot of windows in the playroom and outside was cloudy and then sunny and it became frustrating trying to deal with so I just dialed in 1600 Iso and waited for a cloud to cover the sun. Over all I still am not crazy about the shot but it does make me LAUGH!', '2005-01-19 06:01:56.000000', NULL, 0),
