(1118688, 135260, 6900, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club.</b> <br/> <br/>I am immediately reminded of "On the Verge" when I see this.  I think the biggest difference is focus - there you were focused on your eye and face.  Here you are focused on the dark eye and the one that''s lit up and catches our attention is out of focus.  <br/> <br/>I think the smile distracts from the fear factor as well, because it''s not a "scary smile" but a "jolly" one. :)<br/> <br/>Not much else to talk about here - the negative space is well used and the composition is interesting to look at.  Good luck and happy shooting.<br/> <br/>M<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.  I am immediately reminded of "On the Verge" when I see this.  I think the biggest difference is focus - there you were focused on your eye and face.  Here you are focused on the dark eye and the one that''s lit up and catches our attention is out of focus.   I think the smile distracts from the fear factor as well, because it''s not a "scary smile" but a "jolly" one. :) Not much else to talk about here - the negative space is well used and the composition is interesting to look at.  Good luck and happy shooting. M ', '2005-01-19 08:06:37.000000', NULL, 0),
