(1119168, 134499, 19708, '<td valign="top">Beautiful image Lawrence.<br/>Better title than had you chosen "The Birds".<br/>Congrats on your top twenty finish.</td>', 'Beautiful image Lawrence.Better title than had you chosen "The Birds".Congrats on your top twenty finish.', '2005-01-19 12:54:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1119169, 134178, 4493, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the votes and my second yellow ribbon. <br/> <br/>I should have mentioned that this is a 30 second exposure. That''s what has the water so still. I had originally had a full mirror shot with the light reflecting in the water, when it was suggested to me to crop in so it''s just the dock. Thanks to moodville for that suggestion. It worked out well. Too bad I didn''t realize the ever so slight tilt to the right ;-)<br/> <br/>-danny</td>', 'Thanks for all the votes and my second yellow ribbon.  I should have mentioned that this is a 30 second exposure. That''s what has the water so still. I had originally had a full mirror shot with the light reflecting in the water, when it was suggested to me to crop in so it''s just the dock. Thanks to moodville for that suggestion. It worked out well. Too bad I didn''t realize the ever so slight tilt to the right ;-) -danny', '2005-01-19 12:54:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(1119174, 134000, 19708, '<td valign="top">Superb timing on this image Tim.<br/><i>(wonder if ANY part of Brooklyn looks like this - LOL)</i> <br/>Congrats on a top twenty finish!</td>', 'Superb timing on this image Tim.(wonder if ANY part of Brooklyn looks like this - LOL) Congrats on a top twenty finish!', '2005-01-19 12:57:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(1119205, 134665, 19035, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Kathryn8:</b></div><hr/><i> I was one of those eight that gave this one a 10, it was one of my favorites.  You did a beautiful job and I love the look on the boys face. GREAT! </i></td></tr></table><i></i> <br/> <br/>Thanks so much for the score Kathryn, I appreciate it.</td>', 'Originally posted by Kathryn8: I was one of those eight that gave this one a 10, it was one of my favorites.  You did a beautiful job and I love the look on the boys face. GREAT!   Thanks so much for the score Kathryn, I appreciate it.', '2005-01-19 13:10:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1119225, 134974, 3032, '<td valign="top">Nice to see you entering photos again Nastya. When was the last time, months ago I believe? Should have guessed from the lighting it was you. :)<br/>I don''t know how, but I kept beeing drawn to her eyes. Didn''t even see the wedding ring, like GI Joe noticed. Makes it extra good. :)</td>', 'Nice to see you entering photos again Nastya. When was the last time, months ago I believe? Should have guessed from the lighting it was you. :)I don''t know how, but I kept beeing drawn to her eyes. Didn''t even see the wedding ring, like GI Joe noticed. Makes it extra good. :)', '2005-01-19 13:18:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1119232, 135171, 25133, '<td valign="top">I think you''re stunning. Nice to see a photographer going out on a limb and putting themselves in front of the lens instead of staying behind it!  This was one of my favourites, definetly thought it should have been higher.  But, hey, what do I know?</td>', 'I think you''re stunning. Nice to see a photographer going out on a limb and putting themselves in front of the lens instead of staying behind it!  This was one of my favourites, definetly thought it should have been higher.  But, hey, what do I know?', '2005-01-19 13:21:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(1119237, 134373, 3032, '<td valign="top">Great Photo, shame that it did so poor in the voting.<br/>I don''t think that there are many better ways to put the concept of an actual Phoenix (as a bird) into a photograph without excessive PS. Nice capture. When you shoot the NL, can you see this kind of patterns with your own eyes or does it only materialize after a long exposure?<br/>I have never seen the NL you see. :(</td>', 'Great Photo, shame that it did so poor in the voting.I don''t think that there are many better ways to put the concept of an actual Phoenix (as a bird) into a photograph without excessive PS. Nice capture. When you shoot the NL, can you see this kind of patterns with your own eyes or does it only materialize after a long exposure?I have never seen the NL you see. :(', '2005-01-19 13:22:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1119273, 134230, 20343, '<td valign="top">He''s no Hobo...he actually  works for Schuster&amp;Co. Ecologic in Sibiu, Romania, Europe...</td>', 'He''s no Hobo...he actually  works for Schuster&Co. Ecologic in Sibiu, Romania, Europe...', '2005-01-19 13:32:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1119274, 135197, 25133, '<td valign="top">I gave this one ten, I thought it as very emotive and love the way you got the reflection in the window.  Can''t believe this is you''re first attempt, hopefully you''ll just keep on improving!</td>', 'I gave this one ten, I thought it as very emotive and love the way you got the reflection in the window.  Can''t believe this is you''re first attempt, hopefully you''ll just keep on improving!', '2005-01-19 13:32:44.000000', NULL, 0),
